    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_7ce047c5290618dd579a043bc04cb55811c26cbd200699503e4c69dae4fedfd9",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source supports a staged representation change from an analytic mean square to a localized arithmetic diagonal: Mellin residues express the functional-equation integral through ratio kernels; parity-restricted character orthogonality converts the squared expansion into four-index product congruences; short support removes the negative-congruence competitors and makes the positive congruence an exact product diagonal; common-product and gcd/lcm coordinates then expose coprime factors on which the mollifier's Möbius expansion and a uniform coprime estimate act, leaving an Eulerian arithmetic main sum.",
